# The parameters of the k3s deployment (README.md). Copy this file to
# config.env, which git ignores, and set the values: the Makefile reads it
# and fills them in where the manifests say ${NAME}. A variable on make's
# command line wins over the file. One NAME=value a line, without quotes.

# The DNS zone of the front doors, e.g. example.com: ferund at
# run.<DOMAIN>, FeChat at chat.<DOMAIN>. run.<DOMAIN> is FeRun's trust
# domain too (ferund init-ca).
DOMAIN=

# The registry the images are pushed to and pulled from. Default:
# ghcr.io/gardenlinux/feos, public; a private one needs an
# imagePullSecret added to the manifests.
#REGISTRY=

# The OpenID Connect provider people sign in with to ferund and FeChat,
# exactly as its discovery document states it, e.g. https://id.example.com/.
OIDC_ISSUER=

# The fixed ClusterIP of the service ferund-nodes, which feosd on the
# hosts dials: a free address of the cluster's service network. Default:
# 10.43.70.70, in k3s's default 10.43.0.0/16.
#FERUN_NODES_IP=

# FeChat's model, as the LLM gateway names it.
FECHAT_MODEL=
